{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED for exact head 31ecabce8e93e41ddd9600b3bb3260a99b0f3dad.\n\nThe positional-basis table is accurate, but docs/reference.md:35-50 overgeneralizes it as “the one case where being recorded and having effect come apart.” It is only the unusual citation case at append time. The implementation already proves two temporal cases the requested review named: superseding a role grant removes that role while the grant and ratification decisions remain historically effective; superseding the membership basis removes the participant and every dependent authority while those original decisions likewise remain effective (TestRosterSupersessionRevokesAndResurrectionRestoresAuthority and TestMembershipRevocationRevokesDependentAuthority). The current projection communicates those consequences through statement retired/stale state and Actors/RoleSources, not by rewriting Decisions.\n\nScope the uniqueness claim to admission/citation ordering, and state the temporal rule explicitly: current authority also requires both the grant and its membership basis to remain live; role revocation retires the explicit grant, while membership retirement removes membership and all dependent roles. Tell readers to inspect the current actor/role-source and retired/stale projection rather than the decisions list alone. Without that sentence, a reader following “membership first → role active yes” will generalize incorrectly after revocation.\n\nThe measured three positional rows themselves match addRoleGrant/roleGrantActive. Passed: 29-link check as reported at the head, make vet, make test, make race, make build, make ui reproducibly, and git diff --check. Exact worktree remained clean.","body":{"head":"31ecabce8e93e41ddd9600b3bb3260a99b0f3dad","tests":"29 links; make vet; make test; make race; make build; make ui; git diff --check","verdict":"changes-requested"}}